        <p>COUNTY OF CHESTER. WILD 'BIRDS PROTECTION. NOTICE' Is HEREBY GIVEN, that the follow- ing is a Copy of an ORDER made by the Secretary of State on the 29th day of March, 1901, with reference to the Protection of wild Birds in the Administrative County of Chester, viz. WILD BIRD (ENGLAND). THE WILD BIRDS PROTECTION (COUSTY OF CHESTER) ORDER. 1901. Dated 29th March, 1901.</p>
        <p>In pursuance of the powers conferred on me by the Wild Birds Protection Alts, 1880 to 1898, and upon application by the County Council of the Administrative County of Chester I hereby make the following Order : TITLE.</p>
        <p>I. This Order may be cited as " The Will Birds Protec- tion (County of Chester) Order. 1901." BIRDS. CLOSE TIME EXTENDED.</p>
        <p>11. The time during which the killing or taking of Wild Birds, or any of them, is prohibited by the Act of 1880, shall be extended throughout the County of Chester, so as to be from the 2nd day of March to the 12th day of August in each year. both days inclusive : ADDITIONS TO THE SCHEDULE OF THE ,ACT OF 1880.</p>
        <p>Hi.-" Tb-e Wild Birds Protection Act, 1880, as extended Clause 11. of this Order shall apply within the whole of the County of Chester to the Kestrel and Heron as if those species were included in the Schedule to that Act OTHER ADDLTIONS TO IHE SCHEDULE OF THE ACT OF IEBI.</p>
        <p>IV. The Wild Birds Protection Act, 1880 as extended by Clause 11. of this Order, shall apply within the area named in Clause XI. of this Order to the following species of Wild Birds as if those specien were included in the fechedule to the Act Red-backed Shrike, Whinchat, Spotted Flycatcher, Sedge Warbler, Blackc.p Warbler, Grasshopper Warbler. Wood Warbler, Warden Warbler. Missel Thrush, Common Bunting, Reed Bunting. Goldfinch. Wheatear. Chiffehaff, Golden- crested Wren, Yellow Wagtaii, Pied Wagtail, Water Wagtail, Sky lark, and Titlark. ALL Brims PROTECTED DURING THE WHOLE OF THE YEAR WITHIN A CERTAIN AREA. V.- During that period of the year to which the protection afforded by the Wild Birds Protection Act, 1880 (as extended by Clause II of this Order) does not apply, the killing or taking of Wild Birds is prohibited within the area named in Clause XI of this -Order. ADDITIONAL PROTECTION FOR THE GULL AND TERN. VI. During that period of the year to which the protec- tion afforded by the Wild Birds Protection Act, 1880 (as extended by Clause 11. of this order) does not apply, the killing or taking of the Gull and Tern is prohibited through out the County of Chester. CERTAIN DISTRIers EXEMPTED FROM THE OPERATION ,OF CLAUSE VI. VII. I hereby exerfipt from the operation of Clause VI of this Order so much of the County of Chester as does not lie within the parishes of Puddington, Burton, Ness, Neston- cum-Oldfield, Thurstaston. Oaldy, Hoylake-cum-West Kirby, watiasey, Power Bebingten, Bromborongh Rastham,Hooton. Netherpool, Whitby. Stanlow, Ice. Great btanney, Frod• sham Lordship. Weston. Runcorn, Halton, Norton. Moore, Acton Grange. Walton Inferior. includi-Jg therein so much of the estuaries of the Rivers Dee and Mersey as lies within the Administrative County of Chester, CERTAIN BIRDS PROTECTED DURING THE WHOLE OF THE</p>
      </div>
