        <p>VIII. During that period ot the year to which the pro. tection afforded by " The Wild Birds Protection Act, 1680 " as extended by Clause 11. of this ,rder), does not apply, the killing or taking of the following species of Wild Birds is prohibited throughout the County of Chester : Kingfisher, Great Crested Crehe, Heron, floldfinch. Owl, Siskin, Twite, Brown Linnet, Lesser Rerlpoll, Green Wood. recker, Great Spotted Woodpecker. Lesser Spotted Wood- pecker, Bittern, Shoveller Dusk, L ttle Grebe or Dabchick, Goat Sucker or Nightjar. EGGS.</p>
        <p>CERTAIN BOG + PROTECTED- THROUGHOUT THE COUNTY. IX. The taking or destroying of the Eggs of the follow- ing species of Wild Birds is prohibited thtoughout the County of Chester : Owl, Bit'ern, Kingfisher, Kestral, Heron, She:drake, Dunlin, Blackheaded Gull. Comm,n Tern. Oyster Catsher, Shrike. Hasvfineh. Twite, Green Woodpecker, Great Spotted Woodpecker. Lesscr Spotted Wf oipecker. Little Grebe or Dabchick, Great Crested Grebe, Redshank, Sandpiper. Goat Sucker or Nightjar. ALL HOGS PROTECTED WITHIN A CERTAIN AREA. X. The t ‘lcing or destroying of the eggs of any species of Wild Birds is prohibited within the area named in Clause Xi. for a period of five years from the date of this Order. MARKET GARDEN lawns EXEMPTED FROIYI THE OPERATION</p>
      </div>
      <div type="article" xml:id="PressMint-GB_1903-02-27_WidnesExaminer_art0004" n="art0004">
        <head>OF THIS ORDER.</head>
        <p>OF THIS ORDER.</p>
        <p>XL And I make the fotlowing forther Order, which shall apply within the portion of the hundred of Wirral!. coloured pink on the maps deposited in the Home Office and in the Office of the County Council and embracing ' the low-lying lands and sandhills situate between the estuaries of the Rivers Dee and Mersey, of which the hound- cries shall commence to the south at a point of the main highway of the Coun'y of :Theater 200 yards to the west of the Dock Cottages near " Docks" Railway Station of the Wirral Railway run along the main hiqhway to Bidston Village, and then turn in a northerly direction and run to Bidston Railway Station of the same railway, then turn in a westerly direction and run along the Wirral Railway until it reaches the Meols Station of such railway, then run along the highway near to the Meols Railway Station inn northerly direction to the Irish Sea.then on the north along the margin of high-water mark of the Irish Sea to a point at New Brighton wherethe Yellow Noses joins the said Irish Sea,and then run in a southerly direction to "Warren Drive" or road, and along "Warren Drive" to the most northerly house and cf,unis on the west side of such drive. then along the western boundary of the house and premises situate along the western side of such drive or road to a point 100 yards or so from Grove-road, then turning in a westerly direction along the northern boundaries of the houses and r—emises in Grove-road, Wallasey, until P.; reaches the "'irral Railway, then turning in a southerly direction along the Wirral Railway until it reaches the Wallasey Marsh, then along the edge of the marsh in a southerly direction until it reachea the Poulton Halfpenny Bridge, then turning in a westerly direction on the edge of the said marsh until it reaches along the edge of the marsh the main, highway lead- ing from Poulton to Meols, such parts within the aforesaid boundaries as are market-garden lands and are not coloured in the said mars are excepted from the operation of this Order. REPEAL OF FORMER ORDER.</p>
        <p>XII. The Order of the 15th February, 1898. Is hereby repealed. Given under my hand at Whitehall this 29th day of Marcb,ll9ol. (Signed) CHAS. T. RITCHIF, One of His Maiest.y's Principal Secretaries of State. REGINALD POTTS. Clerk to the Cheshire County„Couneil, Chester.</p>
      </div>
