        <p>Great Sankey School Board. At the monthly meeting of this Board held on Tues- day afternoon there were present ;—Mrs. G. Thomp- son (presiding), the Rev. J. R. Jones, and Messrs. PeAs, W. D. Jeans, Jim. (clerk). and G. Clarke schoolmaster). The Headmasters' report showed an average attendance for the month of 251.3, the total fees being £3 is. 10d.—The Clerk read a letter irom Mr. Joseph Wright, the Chairman of the Board, stating that as he was leaving, the district he wished to resim.his position both as chairman and member. Hentendered his sincere thanks to his co-members for -their kindness and courtesy to him; to those connec- ted with the management of the school, and to the Clerk for the valuable help he had given him during the time he had been associated with the Bcard.The Clerk xemarked that the resignation would take effect in a month, when they would have to elect a new member and chairman.— Mr. Thompson said they regretted very much Mr. Wright's resignation. He moved that the thanks of the Board be given to him for his able conduct in :the chair and for his services —which he believed had extended about 12 years.— Mr. Perks seconded, and the Rev. J. R. Jones suppor- ted, remarking that he had always found Mr. Wright helpful, kind, and courteons..—Mr. Clarke, as master, and on behalf of the staff, expressed regret at Mr. Wright's resignation.—The proposition was carried Warrington Ambulance Men Successful. Warrington ambulance men were very successful in the annual competition taken part in by the teams connected with the Cheshire Lines Railway which took place at the Central Station, Liverpool on Friday evening Mr. David Mel drum presided.—The competing squads, were judged on the basis of the second edition of the official handbook of the association, were—Li- verpool Central, Buskisson Goods, Birkenhead (Shore road), Manchester Central, Warrington Centril, War rington (engineers' department) Warrington (stores department) and Northwich. The prize winners were —l, Warrington Central, 452;2,Warrington (engineers department), 423 ; and Manchester Central, 412, the possible score being 500. The first prize included the challenge cup, smaller cups being presented to the other successful teams. The Chairman, after the dis- tribution of the prizes by Mrs. Meldrun, said it was pleasing to find a steadily growing interest on the part of the men to acquire a knowledge of ambniance work. On the line generally there were 633 ,qualified men, 221 belonging to the traffic department, and 99 to the , engineering department. He hoped the day was not , far off when every platelayer would be so qualified. (Hear hear). On behalf Of the competition committee I Mr.Meldnim presented to Mr. Lloyd a gold scarf pin in recognition of his continued and valuable services The following composed the local teams :—Centra Station : Messrs H. T. Williams, J. Fogg, H. Holloway J. Robertson, and J. Blake. Engineers Department: Messrs J. Newns, J. Lea, W. Newns, J. Tomlinson, and R. Brownbell. This is the sixth time the Station team have won this prize, and the second team have also held theirs twice.</p>
