      <div type="article" xml:id="PressMint-GB_1903-02-27_WidnesExaminer_art0034" n="art0034">
        <head>SMART TAILOR-MADE.</head>
        <p>A SMART TAILOR-MADE.</p>
        <p>many varieties and tones of lace in any large shop, and the prices of which are suited to every purse as they range from a few shillings up to many pounds. Some of us are already possessed of articles of old lace bequeathed to us by our predecessors and hitherto neglected. These can now be employed in many ways according to their nature. as both the deep cape-like collars and bell cuffs of half a century ago are considered the height of the fashion at present. _ _ _</p>
        <p>The smart tailor-made depicted is expressed in one of the new materials, namely a fleckoi canvas. Flecked materials with a rough surface have been much in vogue all winter, and promise to continue high in popular estimation during spring, this variety of canvas being quite the latest style. The coat is of the loose plealed saque order, and the well cut shoulder cape has an exceedingly smart appear- ance. The skirt also is of the latest and most approved cut and mode. Skirts are either kept perfectly plain and cling to the figure just below the waist or are of a very ornate description. I suppose this is brought about by the fact that some women who cannot fail to acknowledge the becomingness of the plain skirt become wearied of the monotony of having all their skirts in the same mode (however graceful it may be), and are, therefore, ready to</p>
