        <p>Improvements Wanted at Bank Quay Station.</p>
        <p>At a meeting of the Council of the Cliamber of Commerce held on Monday under the presidency of the Mayor, it was decided on tie motion of Mr. J. Fairclough, seconded by Mr. F. Monks," That the Secretary be requested to write to the General Man- ager of the London and No rth-Western Railway Com- pany to inquire what plan they had in view as to the inprovement of Bank Quay high level passenger sta- tion, and how soon such improvement will be carried out." The Mayor said the resolution was partly due to a suggeetion made by him at the first meeting. If the station could be improved it would be a great benefit to the town. (Hear, hear.) Councillor Pier- point: There is room for improvement in the pas- senger traffic. j It was decided that the Vice-President of the Chamber (Mr. C. E. Parker) be asked, in the ab- sence of the President, to represent the Chamber at the annual meeting of the Associated Chambers to be held in London on March 3, 4,Eand 5. A further reso- lution was passed also requesting the Secretary (Councillor Bennett) to attend the meeting.</p>
      </div>
