        <p>The draw for the third round of the Cap Competi to: to be played on March 7th, is as follows: Minoru v. Hull. Rochdale Hornets v. Salford. . Runcorn v. Maryport. Hunslet v. Leeds. Bradford v. Oldham. Halifax v. Brighouse Rangers. Barrow V. Batley. K-eighley v. York. .. To be played on Saturday, March 7th.</p>
        <p>the local clubs, Salford and Runcorn are well- while Oldham have a severe task.</p>
        <p>A meeting of the creditors of Sydney H. Nicholls, secretary of the Hull Football Cluj) Limited, was held on Tue,:day at the offices of the Hull Official Receiver. In his report, the Official Receiver stated that the gross liabilities are .4:1,393 and the assets .t3O, the deficiency being, .t1,3g3. Debtor attributed his insol- vency to bad trade and the coal strike at Cardiff, and the receivincr order had been made on his own petition. bi stated that he had formerly been in b usiness as a hotel proprietor at Cardiff. He commenced business in 1890 with a. capital of of 3:250, and he gave up the business in 1900. He was out of employment for twelve months, and was then appointed the paid secre- tray of the Huil Football Club. Thete were no credi- tors present, andlbe matter remains in the hands of the Official Receiver.</p>
        <p>Nicholls is a brother of the famous welsh centr three-quarter and *visited Warrington with the Hull team last season. T believe that" all blacks " hoped once to secure the Welsh skipper through his brother's instrumentality but the deal has not yet come off. •</p>
        <p>Warrington play HO to-day and hope to get an- nother two punts. Last season there would have been no doubt about the matter, but the engagement is recognised as being a severe one this time. With the advantage of ground the home team may-just manage it. Fish will be an absentee again, though he is re- ported fit, and the hal will be the same as on Tues- day. G. Jolley and ht it take the places of Harmer and Warburton in the forwards. The full team is Hallam full back ; Hockenhall, Isherwood, *Dickenson and Harris', three-quarters; Edmunds and Duckworth half back ; Naylor, Edmondson, Forster, J. Swift, W. Swift, G.lJolley, Lunt, and Ashton forwards.</p>
