      <div type="article" xml:id="PressMint-GB_1903-02-27_WidnesExaminer_art0180" n="art0180">
        <head>Foot-Racing.</head>
        <p>Foot-Racing.</p>
        <p>C. J. Straw, a well-known WarrinTton athlete, figured prominently in the .annual contest for the Junior Championsfiip for cross-country running which kook place at Haydock Park on Saturday. Straw ran with the Warrington A.C. who secured the fourth position. Thirty clubs competed for the champion- ship, over a distance of seven miles, Hull Harriers winning with a total of 94 points, Sutton were second with 158 points, and Hollins third with 274. Warrington A.C. were fourth. The first three men were : 1, C. J. Straw, Warrington, 40mins.</p>
